(3389480, 468504, 47852, '<td valign="top">I think some of the other commenters hit on some of the things that would have improved ths shot.  I gave it a 5 personally... it''s something I see all the time when I''m out hiking, and I still haven''t found a unique way to shoot the stuff.  More of a focal point might have helped if there was one really neat section of the fungi perhaps?  Keep submitting.. GO Team D50! :)</td>', 'I think some of the other commenters hit on some of the things that would have improved ths shot.  I gave it a 5 personally... it''s something I see all the time when I''m out hiking, and I still haven''t found a unique way to shoot the stuff.  More of a focal point might have helped if there was one really neat section of the fungi perhaps?  Keep submitting.. GO Team D50! :)', '2007-02-21 12:06:20.000000', NULL, 0),
(3389578, 468420, 47852, '<td valign="top">Ok, I''ll admit, I still don''t really get this one :(  It''s strange that your average of the commenters was only a 3.8... guess the ones that didn''t like it told you so!  They have some valid points, and mostly for me it was not really getting it (but not wanting to claim DNMC), and the odd view of the bird waddling away from you.  It''s a nice convertion to b/w with a nice range of tones though.  Go Team D50! :)</td>', 'Ok, I''ll admit, I still don''t really get this one :(  It''s strange that your average of the commenters was only a 3.8... guess the ones that didn''t like it told you so!  They have some valid points, and mostly for me it was not really getting it (but not wanting to claim DNMC), and the odd view of the bird waddling away from you.  It''s a nice convertion to b/w with a nice range of tones though.  Go Team D50! :)', '2007-02-21 12:17:55.000000', NULL, 0),
