(3391630, 466693, 40386, '<td valign="top">This is the only stage of the Monarch that I dont have.  This is fabulous.  Congrats on the yellow, I hope that I am lucky enough to see one someday as I have a lot of Milkweed plants on our 6 acres and I make sure they dont get cut down.  This is the caterpillar''s staple diet and too many farmers and people are cutting them down.<br/> <br/>Beautiful shot!!  I didnt even notice the reflection until I read your notes.<br/></td>', 'This is the only stage of the Monarch that I dont have.  This is fabulous.  Congrats on the yellow, I hope that I am lucky enough to see one someday as I have a lot of Milkweed plants on our 6 acres and I make sure they dont get cut down.  This is the caterpillar''s staple diet and too many farmers and people are cutting them down. Beautiful shot!!  I didnt even notice the reflection until I read your notes.', '2007-02-21 20:41:46.000000', NULL, 0),
(3391670, 468532, 31399, '<td valign="top">awwwwwwwwww thanks team mates!<br/> <br/>it''s very real Hanae, was just taken AFTER school with one of my students.<br/> <br/>Thanks so very much rinac and jude&gt;  I too thought it exuded SCHOOL biology.  But, I wish I''da gone with the small crop of mostly disection with wet frog...BUT I also liked the community college Tshirt she was wearing (totally accidental) and I left the fuzzy clutter (all things one definetly uses in biology lab) and dof because I felt what Rinac did...threw me right into the frog...alas, sigh, others did not like the DOF at all and wanted the ''clutter'' removed..shrugs...<br/> <br/>love you all!</td>', 'awwwwwwwwww thanks team mates! it''s very real Hanae, was just taken AFTER school with one of my students. Thanks so very much rinac and jude>  I too thought it exuded SCHOOL biology.  But, I wish I''da gone with the small crop of mostly disection with wet frog...BUT I also liked the community college Tshirt she was wearing (totally accidental) and I left the fuzzy clutter (all things one definetly uses in biology lab) and dof because I felt what Rinac did...threw me right into the frog...alas, sigh, others did not like the DOF at all and wanted the ''clutter'' removed..shrugs... love you all!', '2007-02-21 21:06:46.000000', NULL, 0),
(3391847, 468515, 23484, '<td valign="top">I think this is a great idea but it just doesn''t seem to stand out from the background enough. I don''t think contrast would have done much. Maybe a different angle or real shallow DOF.  The clarity is very good.</td>', 'I think this is a great idea but it just doesn''t seem to stand out from the background enough. I don''t think contrast would have done much. Maybe a different angle or real shallow DOF.  The clarity is very good.', '2007-02-21 22:06:46.000000', NULL, 0),
(3392095, 468683, 8891, '<td valign="top">Thanks, Mark, Jeffery (pssst.....change your images per row in your preferences to 7 and it will show up there (it''s number 6), Joe, Cap''n Jen, Jen and Charmayne!  Thanks for all the fine comments during the challenge!</td>', 'Thanks, Mark, Jeffery (pssst.....change your images per row in your preferences to 7 and it will show up there (it''s number 6), Joe, Cap''n Jen, Jen and Charmayne!  Thanks for all the fine comments during the challenge!', '2007-02-21 23:18:30.000000', NULL, 0),
