(3395357, 468483, 72220, '<td valign="top">hey thanks for the comments everyone.  Yes this is trypan blue, which in hindsight, was not the best choice with the background...  The flash was on camera, as I don''t currently have an off-camera flash setup (I do agree that it makes it a bit too harsh).</td>', 'hey thanks for the comments everyone.  Yes this is trypan blue, which in hindsight, was not the best choice with the background...  The flash was on camera, as I don''t currently have an off-camera flash setup (I do agree that it makes it a bit too harsh).', '2007-02-22 20:43:57.000000', NULL, 0),
(3395654, 468532, 811, '<td valign="top">Ewww.  This takes me back to Jr. high. . .I really like your focus on this one.  Typically, the subject is in front and focused, and the background blurred, but this is almost completely reversed.  Nicely done.  I think this would make a cool textbook picture.  I am also hereby declaring you dpc''s most underrated photographer.  All of your pictures are *good* technically, emotionally (that is, they get a response), compositionally, the voters just haven''t discovered you yet.  KEEP SHOOTING, it''s not always the dpc scores that matter.</td>', 'Ewww.  This takes me back to Jr. high. . .I really like your focus on this one.  Typically, the subject is in front and focused, and the background blurred, but this is almost completely reversed.  Nicely done.  I think this would make a cool textbook picture.  I am also hereby declaring you dpc''s most underrated photographer.  All of your pictures are *good* technically, emotionally (that is, they get a response), compositionally, the voters just haven''t discovered you yet.  KEEP SHOOTING, it''s not always the dpc scores that matter.', '2007-02-22 23:00:01.000000', NULL, 0),
